(7335237, 1130909, 173844, '<td valign="top">Flipping about, don''t even know how I chanced upon your image.... it''s beautiful.  My good fortune.</td>', 'Flipping about, don''t even know how I chanced upon your image.... it''s beautiful.  My good fortune.', '2015-03-29 11:39:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(7424457, 1130744, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>Apologies for the long delayed critique. I like your image it is very busy and cluttered but in a constructive sort of way, everything seems to add to the whole. I particularly like the recurring reflections in the phone though I wish the detail were better, the blown highlights are detrimental in a key area of your image. The edge of the screen and the batten behind the phone are also a little over-exposed and dominating but not excessively so. I quite like the processing I think it has added another element to the image. The only thing that is a little unfortunate is the positioning of the cat against the background image it is sufficiently similar in colour that it appears to give the cat an unnatural square look. Overall, a good result.<br/> <br/>Thank you for your entry Fe, hope you had a lovely festive holiday and a creative New Year to you.</td>', 'Hello from the Critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge Apologies for the long delayed critique. I like your image it is very busy and cluttered but in a constructive sort of way, everything seems to add to the whole. I particularly like the recurring reflections in the phone though I wish the detail were better, the blown highlights are detrimental in a key area of your image. The edge of the screen and the batten behind the phone are also a little over-exposed and dominating but not excessively so. I quite like the processing I think it has added another element to the image. The only thing that is a little unfortunate is the positioning of the cat against the background image it is sufficiently similar in colour that it appears to give the cat an unnatural square look. Overall, a good result. Thank you for your entry Fe, hope you had a lovely festive holiday and a creative New Year to you.', '2015-12-28 08:12:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(7424536, 1130691, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Hmm....this is one of those pics that make you go...waitaminute...things look a little too perfect, a little too in place...then I saw your photog''s notes and saw that you did indeed shoot a window display, someone else''s work.  The lighting has that peculiar flatness to it that you tend to see in store window displays, which was also a tip-off. I think the crop is a little tight and voters don''t usually like portrait crops.  The title is a little ambiguous too, which doesn''t help.<br/> <br/>Ok. Got that out of my system!  This was a free study, so of course anything goes. The skeleton dominates the pic but the lanterns clustered around the head draw the eye away a bit, almost to the point of not noticing the pumpkin at the end of the arm.  I like the fog effect. That, and a whole lotta dodge and burn, could have been put to use to maximize and minimize the impact of all the various elements here. And it all would have been legal under Advanced!<br/> <br/>Hope this has been helpful<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Hmm....this is one of those pics that make you go...waitaminute...things look a little too perfect, a little too in place...then I saw your photog''s notes and saw that you did indeed shoot a window display, someone else''s work.  The lighting has that peculiar flatness to it that you tend to see in store window displays, which was also a tip-off. I think the crop is a little tight and voters don''t usually like portrait crops.  The title is a little ambiguous too, which doesn''t help. Ok. Got that out of my system!  This was a free study, so of course anything goes. The skeleton dominates the pic but the lanterns clustered around the head draw the eye away a bit, almost to the point of not noticing the pumpkin at the end of the arm.  I like the fog effect. That, and a whole lotta dodge and burn, could have been put to use to maximize and minimize the impact of all the various elements here. And it all would have been legal under Advanced! Hope this has been helpful Susan', '2015-12-28 21:51:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(7424540, 1131101, 150277, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>I have mixed feelings when looking at this image.  The dynamic range seems really good - I like how the images shows very dark darkness and very white brightness.  The composition is nice, I like the symmetry of the waterway and the ''island'' provides a nice central item for the eye to land on.  But I missed color in the image, the darkness was a bit much dark for me and I kept thinking ''cemetary'' for some reason.  <br/> <br/>This scored well in the challenge, so you connected highly with a number of voters.  Well done with that! To get the kind of range and detail from a cell phone image is pretty cool.  Great choice for the challenge.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. I have mixed feelings when looking at this image.  The dynamic range seems really good - I like how the images shows very dark darkness and very white brightness.  The composition is nice, I like the symmetry of the waterway and the ''island'' provides a nice central item for the eye to land on.  But I missed color in the image, the darkness was a bit much dark for me and I kept thinking ''cemetary'' for some reason.   This scored well in the challenge, so you connected highly with a number of voters.  Well done with that! To get the kind of range and detail from a cell phone image is pretty cool.  Great choice for the challenge.', '2015-12-28 23:07:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(7424542, 1131013, 150277, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>Well, this was one of my favorites from this challenge, which always makes a critique more challenging.  I loved the colors in the sky and the symmetry provided by the reflection.  The near silhouette made the image very real for me.  I liked the spread of trees through the whole image, but I suppose if I have to find something I thought might be a weakness, the right side of the image seemed a bit heavier with those larger trees and the movement of the clouds seem to stop over on the right.  (My brain is very concrete, so likes complete symmetry a lot, the little tree on the far left just didn''t stand out as strongly as the other trees.)<br/> <br/>But you scored very highly in the challenge, and during voting I thought this was a very strong image and was really well done.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. Well, this was one of my favorites from this challenge, which always makes a critique more challenging.  I loved the colors in the sky and the symmetry provided by the reflection.  The near silhouette made the image very real for me.  I liked the spread of trees through the whole image, but I suppose if I have to find something I thought might be a weakness, the right side of the image seemed a bit heavier with those larger trees and the movement of the clouds seem to stop over on the right.  (My brain is very concrete, so likes complete symmetry a lot, the little tree on the far left just didn''t stand out as strongly as the other trees.) But you scored very highly in the challenge, and during voting I thought this was a very strong image and was really well done.', '2015-12-28 23:16:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(7424590, 1131046, 86447, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club, Max!<br/> <br/>This is so simple and so stunning and yet... some never see it. They/we pass right by.  Well done!<br/> <br/>I like the composition and the clarity/sharpness of the drops.  I''m not as fond of the odd color you''ve chosen.   But, I''m not sure it would be as good in BW.  So... perhaps less saturation and a different hue?<br/> <br/>Anyway, it got 8th place and a good score, so take my opinion with a grain of salt. :D<br/> <br/>I wish you''d come enter again... I love your style.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club, Max! This is so simple and so stunning and yet... some never see it. They/we pass right by.  Well done! I like the composition and the clarity/sharpness of the drops.  I''m not as fond of the odd color you''ve chosen.   But, I''m not sure it would be as good in BW.  So... perhaps less saturation and a different hue? Anyway, it got 8th place and a good score, so take my opinion with a grain of salt. :D I wish you''d come enter again... I love your style. ', '2015-12-29 12:06:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(7424697, 1131167, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Geodesic domes are always fun to see at nighttime as they are invariably lit up in some way to draw attention to them.  Composition is interesting with the silhouetted palms and then the huge colourful dome behind them. Not cropped too closely and seeing that this was probably shot handheld, very good for 1/15th of a second. The pic itself is a nice informal study of the EPCOT Centre, but there just isn''t a real wow factor here to captivate the voters.<br/> <br/>Hope this has been helpful<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Geodesic domes are always fun to see at nighttime as they are invariably lit up in some way to draw attention to them.  Composition is interesting with the silhouetted palms and then the huge colourful dome behind them. Not cropped too closely and seeing that this was probably shot handheld, very good for 1/15th of a second. The pic itself is a nice informal study of the EPCOT Centre, but there just isn''t a real wow factor here to captivate the voters. Hope this has been helpful Susan', '2015-12-29 20:19:09.000000', NULL, 0);
